  "behavior": [
    "Copy construction shares the source base message and stack without recapturing a stack trace.",
    "The constructed object has Standard_Failure identity even when the source is a derived exception.",
    "The constructed object omits Standard_OutOfMemory private storage and uses the source base message, not its virtual what() value."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Pinned native source messages can contain arbitrary nonzero bytes. A native-only diagnostic roundtrips byte 0xff with shared message storage; Rust Failure base fields are Arc<str> and cannot represent that state. The row stays partial.",
    "Two Rust supplemental tests cover the representable derived-source cases. The native-only byte diagnostic is not counted as a passing Rust parity case.",
    "Ordinary Clone remains whole-value Rust copying; the copy constructor maps to explicit copy_base.",
    "No original legacy declarations added."
  ],
